time, ostensibly to focus on her songwriting. When she throws herself into composing music for days on end, the results tend to fall in one of two categories: either something extraordinarily beautiful or extraordinarily bizarre.\n\n\"This... is a song celebrating the birth of a new hero. Someone with the courage to fight alongside the weak — strong, yet humble and kind... It's dedicated to my heroes: Evan and Karin.\""},"used_in":[{"tip":"Raid: Destroyer Gaze","cat":"pve","banner":"RAID_DG.webp"},{"tip":"Adventure (Both)","cat":"pve","banner":"ADVENTURE_BOTH.webp"},{"tip":"Sudden Raid: Calistra","cat":"pve","banner":"RAID_SUDDEN_CALISTRA.webp"},{"tip":"Power Up Dungeon","cat":"pve","banner":"PU_DUNGEON.webp"},{"tip":"Infinite Tower","cat":"pve","banner":"INFINITE_TOWER.webp"},{"tip":"Castle Rush","cat":"pve","banner":"CR_ALL.webp"},{"tip":"Tower of Trials","cat":"pve","banner":"TOWER_OF_TRIALS.webp"},{"tip":"Advent Expedition: Kyle & Karma","cat":"pve","banner":"ADVENT_KYLEKARMA.webp"}],"lore":"Yui was born to a pair of bards in a small village in Dragon Ruins.\nEven from a young age, she'd often wander from town to town on her father's heels. During these journeys, she'd often get caught up in her daydreams and wander off the path. This rather dangerous tendency ended up fostering something much greater: an innate talent for telling stories.\nThis led to her striking out on her own at a young age to make her own songs. Since she was well-travelled and well-mannered, it was quite easy for her to capture hearts in every town she visited.\nBoth of her parents died an early and unfortunate death. She stepped in to fill their void as the singing voice in their troupe.\nShe was rescued by Evan's crew in the Blazing Desert while on the way back to her hometown. Their meeting there was brief, but they met again at Dragon Ruins, where the crew helped to save her adoptive hometown.\nShe joined the Evan Expedition out of a sense of gratitude. She recorded all of their exploits into song, which have come to be widely regarded as the most accurate primary source of the events that transpired."}